; The seeded-random family is the one place in the evaluator where
; "deterministic" is the entire feature. Every one of these is a pure
; function of (seed, key, …) over a vendored SplitMix64, with no hidden
; state and no platform entropy — which is a claim the corpus is the only
; thing that can actually check, because it replays these exact digits
; through the native build, `sjon.wasm` under Node, and `sjon.wasm` under
; wasmtime.
;
; Forms 0-2 pin `hash` itself, and pin that both inputs matter: changing
; the key (form 1) and changing the seed (form 2) each move the result to
; somewhere unrelated. Forms 3/4 are `rand01` over the same two hashes, so
; the two layers are pinned independently — a change to the hash and a
; compensating change to the float derivation cannot cancel out unnoticed.
;
; Forms 6-9 are the derived generators at one shared (seed, key), so they
; are all reading the same underlying draw: `rand-int` lands on 3 in
; [1, 6], `rand-choice` picks :b out of three, and `rand-bool` at that
; draw is true at p = 0.5. Forms 8/9 pin the two saturating ends —
; p = 0 is never true and p = 1 always is, whatever the draw was.
(hash 1 0)
(hash 1 1)
(hash 2 0)
(rand01 1 0)
(rand01 1 1)
(rand-range 7 3 -1.0 1.0)
(rand-int 7 3 1 6)
(rand-bool 7 3 0.5)
(rand-bool 7 3 0.0)
(rand-bool 7 3 1.0)
(rand-choice 7 3 [:a :b :c])
